lesson k-looking-after-living-things v=1 format=teach grade=0 unit=9 subject=nature levels=[easy, medium, hard] {
  title "Looking after living things"
  goal "Say what a plant or a pet needs from us each day."

  look {
    scene 14x8 {
      rabbits r count=2 facing=1 at=canvas(1, 1)
    }
    say """
        Living things need looking after. A plant needs water, light and room to grow. A pet needs food,
        fresh water, a safe home, exercise and gentle hands. We wash our hands after we hold an animal.
      """
  }
  do {
    level easy {
      worked k.what-plant-needs k=0 level=medium
    }
    practice k.what-plant-needs count=2 seed=2
    practice k.pet-care count=3 seed=3 easy-count=2
    practice k.count-the-pets count=2 seed=4 easy-count=1
    show k.care-promise
  }
  try stars=2 {
    show k.too-much-water
  }
  try stars=3 {
    show k.care-plan
  }
  remember {
    say "Plants and animals need us to give them what they need, gently, every day."
  }

  grown-ups """
    Read each question aloud. Growing things named what a seed needs; this lesson is the step on
    from it, the child taking care of a living thing day after day. The plant job runs over a week
    and is for you to watch. If the child is stuck, ask how they would feel without water or food.
    Never leave a child alone with an animal. Off the page, give the child one small daily job for a
    plant or a pet. Japan, 幼稚園教育要領 (kindergarten guidelines), 環境, 内容 (5):
    "身近な動植物に親しみをもって接し，生命の尊さに気付き，いたわったり，大切にしたりする。" (Treat familiar
    animals and plants with affection, notice that life is precious, and care for it.)
    """
  level easy {
    grown-ups "At this level dry soil is worked in the teacher's pen first, the plant needs water or light, and there are two or three rabbits."
  }
  level hard {
    grown-ups "At this level the plant needs room or a holiday helper, the pet questions include food that harms, and there are five or six rabbits."
  }
}
